1.3    Assumptions and Justifications
    微




To streamline the problem and facilitate the simulation of real-life conditions, we have
made several fundamental assumptions. These assumptions have been carefully justi-
fied.
    • Assumption: The water flow between Lake Michigan and Lake Huron does
      not influence our model
    • Justification: According to the data given in the Addendum, the water level of
      Lake Michigan and that of Lake Huron are the same.
