ders Dam to align with the heightened runoff from the Ottawa River poses a risk of
flooding in Montreal. Therefore, there is a crucial necessity to collaboratively regulate




                                                            els
the runoff from both rivers, ensuring the safety not only of Montreal but also of the
                               号
shoreline of Lake Ontario.




                                                          od
   (2) Establishment of a sensible stakeholder weighting is essential (and it should
vary seasonally). For instance, during the spring and summer months, a higher weight-
